{
  "email": "tom.becker@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Find the quarantined scan email and its quarantine reason"
}

{
  "user_id": 4,
  "reason": "Account shows locked with 5 failed logins; check for suspicious activity given malware email targeting user"
}

{
  "summary": "Reported: Tom Becker (Finance, user_id 4) asked us to release a quarantined \"scanned document zip\" he believes came from the office copier. Checked: his quarantine. Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", received 2026-10-09 21:18 UTC, was quarantined as MALWARE and is not releasable. The sender is an external domain, not our internal copier, and this is a typical malware lure (fake scanner notice with a zip). NOT released. Because it was caught in quarantine, the user has not received or opened it. Please have security review it and block the sender/domain across the org, and check whether other users got the same message. Other items: Q-1004 (Harborview Supplies invoice, spam, releasable) is also in his quarantine; he did not ask about it. His account is currently LOCKED after 5 failed passwords on 2026-10-09 09:20-09:35 ET. All of those came from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York, mixed in with a successful Duo sign-in, and there are no hosting-network or foreign sign-ins. This looks like the user mistyping his password, not a compromise. He hasn't asked for an unlock. Still needed: security review/block of the sender, and if he has real copier scans missing, a check of the internal scan-to-email path.",
  "reason": "Requested message is marked malware; KB-007/KB-008 require escalation for security review"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the email you mean (\"Scanned document 0931.zip\"), but we can't release it. Our mail filter marked it as malware, and it came from an outside address (docs-share), not from our office copier. Fake \"scanned document\" emails with zip files are a common way to spread malware. It was stopped before it reached you, so you're safe. Please don't open any copies of it you see elsewhere. I've passed it to our security team to review and block the sender. If you're expecting real scans from the copier, try scanning again or let us know which copier you used, and we'll check why they aren't coming through. Also, a heads-up: your account is locked right now after several wrong password attempts on Friday morning. If you need it unlocked, just reply and we'll take care of it.",
  "internal_note": "Quarantine check: Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", reason malware, not releasable. External look-alike scanner lure, not our internal copier. Not released, per KB-007/KB-008. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation #1) to review and block the sender org-wide. Q-1004 (Harborview invoice, spam, releasable) is also in quarantine; the user didn't ask about it. Account is LOCKED after 5 failed passwords on 10/09 09:20-09:35 ET, all from corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York with a Duo success mixed in. No hosting or foreign sign-ins, so this looks like the user mistyping, not a compromise. No unlock requested; I offered one to the user.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
